.TH "SPGEN-AGGREGATE" "1" "" "spgen 0.1.0" ""
.SH NAME
spgen\-aggregate \- Generates the aggregate module with apply/2 clauses per event
.SH SYNOPSIS
mix sp.gen.aggregate [options] <AGGREGATE|COMMAND|EVENT>
.SH DESCRIPTION
The stream of events for one domain object, folded into state.
.SH Prerequisite
.IP \[bu] 2
The Domain Model (../../../../domain\-model/README.md) contains the aggregate and the events that change it.
.PP
The generator accepts an aggregate, command or event element and always resolves the aggregate's own element, so mix sp.gen.aggregate position and mix sp.gen.aggregate catalog\-position write the same file.
.SH "What the generator does"
.IP \[bu] 2
typedstruct state from the aggregate's state.
.IP \[bu] 2
One apply/2 clause per event of the constituent, pattern\-matching aggregate and event: a create rebuilds the struct from the event's fields, an update merges Event.get_changes/1, a delete returns nil.
.IP \[bu] 2
The @moduledoc, which stays a TODO: marker until the model describes the aggregate.
.SH Tests
The aggregate's describe "Aggregate" lives in the event test (./event\-test.md), one applies <event> to aggregate state case per event: create starts from an empty struct, update seeds the id, delete asserts nil. Field\-by\-field assertions follow the event's data.
.SS "Generated files"
.IP \[bu] 2
services/api/lib/sportipedia/<_subdomain>/<composite>/<domain_object>/aggregate.ex (typedstruct state with apply clauses)
.IP \[bu] 2
services/api/test/sportipedia/<_subdomain>/<composite>/<domain_object>/events/<_event>_test.exs (aggregate fold test per event)
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-subdomain\fR \fI<SUBDOMAIN>\fR

.TP
\fB\-\-composite\fR \fI<COMPOSITE>\fR

.TP
\fB\-\-constituent\fR \fI<CONSTITUENT>\fR

.TP
\fB\-\-model\fR \fI<MODEL>\fR
model root, default docs/domain\-model (relative to \-\-root)
.TP
\fB\-\-root\fR \fI<ROOT>\fR
repo root, default inferred from the current directory
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
report the drift, write nothing
.TP
\fB\-f\fR, \fB\-\-force\fR
FE: rewrite present generated units in place
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIAGGREGATE|COMMAND|EVENT\fR>
the element: esdm: reference, *.esdm.yaml, kind.name, or bare name
.SH "SEE ALSO"
spgen(1)
suites: operation, feature
